On Tue, Mar 9, 2010 at 10:20 PM, <lojban@st-andrews.ac.uk> wrote:

>
> Hello all;
>
>  I have recently started a student society centred around Lojban at the
> University of St. Andrews, here in Scotland; I thought someone on this list
> might be interested/happy/intrigued to know about us.
>
>  We're meeting once a week at the pub to discuss Lojban. Right now we're
> just
> moving through Lojban for Beginners, but in the future we hope to discuss
> tricky grammar points, share original works, and provide support for St.
> Andrews students undertaking Lojban-related projects.
>
>  Having sent some blanket emails to the departments, we've received some
> level
> of interest from about 25 people, about 10 of whom have actually shown up
> for a
> meeting. Although we've only had 5 meetings so far, the first 2 of which
> weren't
> publicly advertised, so maybe this isn't too bad.
>
>  I can't imagine anyone (outside St. Andrews) reaping any huge benefit from
> our
> existence; nevertheless, I encourage ya'll to contact us with questions,
> comments, ideas, words of encouragement, Lojbanic inspiration, good
> cocktail
> recipes, etc.
>

